WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.590
- So, a Florida woman was arrested

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:04.590
for calling 911 more than 12,000 times.

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:06.120
I mean, I guess the only thing worse

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.130
than calling the police
and them not helping you

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.590
is calling the police over 12,000 times

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.480
and them not helping you.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.970
This particular woman
called over 500 times

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.950
in just one 24-hour period.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.240
Look, I get it.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.940
You're not a fan of the police. Fair.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.150
But 12,000 calls is probably excessive.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.920
Police officials said
that her calls accounted

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.290
for 12% of incoming traffic

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.090
at that particular police department.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.650
The criminal complaint against this woman

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.110
includes a bunch of First
Amendment protected activity.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.080
It says she continuously
calls, harasses, belittles,

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.640
swears at, argues with,

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.010
and demands officers come arrest her.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.660
Then she refuses to answer the door,

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.670
has in the past given
officers the middle finger

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.140
and screams at them through the windows.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.590
And while flipping off
the police is not a crime,

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.470
making thousands of false 911 calls is.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.060
But at least here we have a happy outcome

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:57.210
because after 12,000 calls,
she was arrested again,

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.593
just as she requested.

